  "migration": "3011e61 feat(viewer): replace the LRU-40 bitmap cache with LFUDA-40",
  "captured_from": "the real pre-migration viewer bundle (LruCache) at commit 1ed4857, run by scripts/measure_cache.mjs against a live server on the published ESO pyramids for images 4, 5 and 6. Measured, not simulated.",
  "why_data_only": "LRU is not a production option in this repository and is not reimplemented for benchmarking. These numbers are preserved as evidence and are compared against by scripts/cache_workload_benchmark.cjs.",
  "not_reproducible": "The LRU bundle no longer exists, so these exact numbers cannot be regenerated. They are evidence from one session, not a protocol requirement.",
  "harness": {
    "name": "measure_cache.mjs (pre-migration, external to the repository)",
    "pacing": "sleep-paced: each viewport step awaited a settle window",
    "step_tiles": 2,
    "calibration_grid": "2^(-7 + i*0.2) for i in 0..90, first maximum of visibleTileRange(effective).length where effective == desired",
    "bug": "recenter() passed (anchor - camera) to a pointermove handler that subtracts the delta, so it reflected the camera about the anchor instead of moving it to the anchor",
    "re_fetch_definition": "a TILE frame is a re-fetch when its image:z:x:y key was already successfully transferred earlier in the session; counted from the wire, not from the cache counters. The history is never reset, so the image-switch-out-and-back trace is included.",
    "image_switch_history": "included (see re_fetch_definition)",
    "lfu_age": "0 (LRU has no aging watermark)"
  },
  "comparison_caveat": "NOT workload-comparable to scripts/cache_workload_benchmark.cjs. In these runs three of the nine traces are degenerate: 'small back-and-forth x10', 'serpentine 6 cols x 5 rows' and 'wide sweep 20 steps' each record zero misses, zero evictions and zero re-fetches, together about 51 of the ~128 viewport operations. The recorded wantAfter of 6 for the latter two shows why: the camera ended up parked in a clipped image corner where a two-tile step keeps revisiting the same handful of tiles. The cause is a sign error in the pre-migration harness, whose recenter passed (anchor - camera) to a handler that SUBTRACTS the delta, reflecting the camera about the anchor instead of moving it there. Reproducing that reflection in the canonical harness does reproduce the degenerate all-hits 'small back-and-forth' trace, but not the whole historical camera path, so the exact historical session has not been reproduced. The canonical harness recenters correctly, which makes its workload harder: it explores roughly 50 percent more tiles per session. Read these numbers as evidence about one session, never as an LFUDA-versus-LRU verdict.",
  "internal_validity": "The LFUDA and LRU runs here were produced by the SAME harness in the same session shape, so their mutual comparison is internally consistent. What it does not support is a claim about a realistic navigation workload, because roughly 40 percent of the operations contributed nothing to it.",
